[[:db/retract 17592186124890 :question/answer-fields 17592186121940] {:db/id 17592186124553 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-af624627-f936-5c7e-a5ee-772c5d7da48f" "question-563f43ed-8e03-5890-8ba0-fe3a95b9c80d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124287 :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{x^2+2y^2-2}{x^2}$ are given by $f(x,y) = c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=1$ gives a circle\n\nII. $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n\nIII. $c=2$ gives a hyperbola" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c5ccf563-8a57-5f1f-ad06-ef72dc726ab7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-af624627-f936-5c7e-a5ee-772c5d7da48f" :question/id #uuid "af624627-f936-5c7e-a5ee-772c5d7da48f" :question/math-academy-id "q-128448" :question/problem "What is the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $P(3,-1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2}{x-y}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,-1) & =\\frac{2}{3-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $P(3,-1)$ is the $\\frac{1}{2}$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{2}{x-y} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 4 & =x-y \\\\ y & =x-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $P(3,-1)$ is the line $y=x-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-11ea0465-98a8-532d-bb2d-293a976cf74c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-11ea0465-98a8-532d-bb2d-293a976cf74c" :answer-field/id #uuid "11ea0465-98a8-532d-bb2d-293a976cf74c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9a0b0721-1fd0-5994-a36a-82e40db9769c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-44caf6b5-57f9-522a-a950-aba744b9e3c3" "answer-cc8a8126-4229-53cd-bece-781ab226e64b" "answer-0329b153-bf57-5eea-8e4f-f3f01337857b" "answer-6d6f7295-9d6c-517b-9e6e-6ee1b2c02c7e" "answer-9a0b0721-1fd0-5994-a36a-82e40db9769c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44caf6b5-57f9-522a-a950-aba744b9e3c3" :answer/id #uuid "44caf6b5-57f9-522a-a950-aba744b9e3c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc8a8126-4229-53cd-bece-781ab226e64b" :answer/id #uuid "cc8a8126-4229-53cd-bece-781ab226e64b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0329b153-bf57-5eea-8e4f-f3f01337857b" :answer/id #uuid "0329b153-bf57-5eea-8e4f-f3f01337857b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d6f7295-9d6c-517b-9e6e-6ee1b2c02c7e" :answer/id #uuid "6d6f7295-9d6c-517b-9e6e-6ee1b2c02c7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a0b0721-1fd0-5994-a36a-82e40db9769c" :answer/id #uuid "9a0b0721-1fd0-5994-a36a-82e40db9769c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-563f43ed-8e03-5890-8ba0-fe3a95b9c80d" :question/id #uuid "563f43ed-8e03-5890-8ba0-fe3a95b9c80d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128450" :question/problem "What is the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $P(-2,-1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2,-1) & =4{(-2)}^{2}+9{(-1)}^{2} \\\\  & =4(4)+9(1) \\\\  & =16+9 \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $P(-2,-1)$ is the $25$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=25.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $P(-2,-1)$ is the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=25.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-30fcae88-a1e2-5970-b696-299270bb46fe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-30fcae88-a1e2-5970-b696-299270bb46fe" :answer-field/id #uuid "30fcae88-a1e2-5970-b696-299270bb46fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-000302c2-3c84-5577-bb85-c11cc3bf9cee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-000302c2-3c84-5577-bb85-c11cc3bf9cee" "answer-0bb60a10-e100-54a3-a098-70fb2ea763e7" "answer-df1cdfb6-d415-5196-8163-5b0778c79a74" "answer-a513aedd-cbc7-5326-bb5e-498f3f229294" "answer-6df11da8-be9b-5344-b62d-79a4559efa3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-000302c2-3c84-5577-bb85-c11cc3bf9cee" :answer/id #uuid "000302c2-3c84-5577-bb85-c11cc3bf9cee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bb60a10-e100-54a3-a098-70fb2ea763e7" :answer/id #uuid "0bb60a10-e100-54a3-a098-70fb2ea763e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df1cdfb6-d415-5196-8163-5b0778c79a74" :answer/id #uuid "df1cdfb6-d415-5196-8163-5b0778c79a74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a513aedd-cbc7-5326-bb5e-498f3f229294" :answer/id #uuid "a513aedd-cbc7-5326-bb5e-498f3f229294" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6df11da8-be9b-5344-b62d-79a4559efa3c" :answer/id #uuid "6df11da8-be9b-5344-b62d-79a4559efa3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186262933 :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+{y}^{2}}{x}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=-1$ gives a line\n\nII. $c=0$ gives a parabola, excluding the origin\n\nIII. $c=1$ gives the $x$-axis, excluding the origin" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124890 :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}+1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n\nII. $c=2$ gives a parabola\n\nIII. $c=3$ gives an ellipse" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186402427 :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=xy$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n\nII. $c=-1$ gives a parabola\n\nIII. $c=0$ gives the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-c5ccf563-8a57-5f1f-ad06-ef72dc726ab7" :question/id #uuid "c5ccf563-8a57-5f1f-ad06-ef72dc726ab7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129114" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)={y}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ {y}^{2} & =c \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equations $y=\\pm \\sqrt{c}$ do not depend on $x.$ So, for a given $c\\in [0,\\infty ),$ the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of horizontal lines, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3c/3c44ae1b59af6ac6f64efedcf4242aaad07ddcf98c2b63c4aeae7958a6622874.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-adf8aa6a-75ee-5eec-b556-6b1e3d610f4a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-adf8aa6a-75ee-5eec-b556-6b1e3d610f4a" :answer-field/id #uuid "adf8aa6a-75ee-5eec-b556-6b1e3d610f4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-19118c24-d5da-5954-9e93-75cfa8bacbe5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ea4ea415-1a42-5ab9-a4f6-74d5d9c47e2c" "answer-19118c24-d5da-5954-9e93-75cfa8bacbe5" "answer-b68c227f-79b4-539e-9f21-17aa72aae1be" "answer-f049c9a7-cc49-5c3f-a4df-0714b2f9933a" "answer-d4fdc308-acd9-599d-98f4-61b51923dcf4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea4ea415-1a42-5ab9-a4f6-74d5d9c47e2c" :answer/id #uuid "ea4ea415-1a42-5ab9-a4f6-74d5d9c47e2c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/08/0857b5d843c6d3f5ca6218ee0f27fe169aedc59676b245578bc8db21fabe6178.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19118c24-d5da-5954-9e93-75cfa8bacbe5" :answer/id #uuid "19118c24-d5da-5954-9e93-75cfa8bacbe5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/3c/3c44ae1b59af6ac6f64efedcf4242aaad07ddcf98c2b63c4aeae7958a6622874.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b68c227f-79b4-539e-9f21-17aa72aae1be" :answer/id #uuid "b68c227f-79b4-539e-9f21-17aa72aae1be" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/3f/3fde41d8d88f0d843e80ae813b07ec030502bcbaa060bc5d54ade4f5207a8740.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f049c9a7-cc49-5c3f-a4df-0714b2f9933a" :answer/id #uuid "f049c9a7-cc49-5c3f-a4df-0714b2f9933a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/c6/c6a799db8c86ff2bfb702dbba92f8d26011d33016aa33f5df1b4a58601205f04.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4fdc308-acd9-599d-98f4-61b51923dcf4" :answer/id #uuid "d4fdc308-acd9-599d-98f4-61b51923dcf4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ca/ca10c21bb658bc3075d0d66321d888c2b23596c1416f605ab0bb8cf79c40af24.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124702 :activity/expected-seconds 